Normally, this will not have italic correction, but here it does; why?

|    \textit{half}. | \textit{half}.

Compare:

|{\itshape half\/}. | {\itshape half\/}. (wrong; but what |\textit| produces)

|  {\itshape half}. | {\itshape half}. (right; and what |\textit| does
everywhere else)

